<h3 class="font-headline-sm text-primary">Oral Antibiotic Treatment</h3>
</div>
<ul class="space-y-6">
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Mild Cellulitis</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Amoxicillin-clavulanate for 10–14 days. For penicillin allergy, clindamycin or azithromycin. Patients must show improvement within 48–72 hours or be escalated to IV treatment.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Moderate Cellulitis</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Initial IV antibiotics in hospital for 24–48 hours, followed by oral antibiotics to complete a 14-day course. Elevation of the affected area and warm compresses accelerate recovery.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 md:p-12 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6 pb-6 border-b border-surface-variant">
